{"type":"message","id":"d61beb48","parentId":"f23eb6be","timestamp":"2026-05-30T16:15:50.009Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both `Authorization: Bearer` and `X-API-Key` return Unauthorized, but the GET requests worked with `X-API-Key`. Let me try a different approach - maybe the POST needs different formatting or the endpoint is different. Let me check if there's a different send endpoint or if I need to include the API key differently.\n\nActually wait - the GET worked with X-API-Key header. But POST with same header gives error code 1101 (not Unauthorized). The error code 1101 might be a Cloudflare Workers error or a specific platform error.\n\nLet me try without the -s flag to see full output, and try different content types or body formats.\n","thinkingSignature":"2cbf548906102157138170905aa84b73d19efbd8b7c54f5703f4aea8e7c4242d"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_a01ho0ew9dy5_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d \"{\\\"threadId\\\":\\\"arbitration\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"heartbeat test\\\"}\" -v 2>&1 | tail -30"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":129,"output":233,"cacheRead":19964,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20326,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780157740309,"responseId":"066a402c75b9a5b9a33d93bc021b4052"}}
